('CIT_DIO_DEACONS_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_DEACONS','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 5','life, and carry themselves illustriously in dispensing Thy celestial mysteries : through Deacons, who are modest, and perform the pure and royal ministry without flaw, through true, faithful ones, who occupy themselves in words and acts worthy of a Christian ; through choirs of virgins of each sex, bearing about in their members the life- giving mortification of Thy Only-begotten Son.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 1','For sketch of Life, Internal Evidence of date, and External Testimony to genuineness during first nine centuries, see " Celestial and Ecclesiastical Hierarchy." (Skeffington, 25. &amp;/.) DIONYSIUS THE AREOPAGITE ON THE HEAVENLY HIERARCHY. CAPUT I. To MY FELLOW PRESBYTER TIMOTHY*. DIONYSIUS THE PRESBYTER. That every divine illumination, whilst going forth lovingly to the objects of its forethought under various forms, remains simplex. Nor is this all.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_HIERARCHS_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_HIERARCHS','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 5','But the illuminating Rank of the Priests conducts those, who are being initiated under the Rank of the inspired Hierarchs, to the on the Ecclesiastical Hierarchy. 129 Divine visions of the Mystic Rites, and in co-opera tion with it, ministers its proper ministrations.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_MONKS_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_MONKS','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 6','149 to God; but if he belonged to the rank of the chaste Monks, or the holy people, he lays him down near the hallowed sanctuary, before the sacerdotal en trance. Then the Hierarch finishes the prayer of thanksgiving to God ; and next, the Leitourgoi, after reading the unfailing promises concerning our holy resurrection, contained in the Divine Oracles, rever ently chant the odes of the same teaching and power, from the Oracles of the Psalter k.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_PRIESTS_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_PRIESTS','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 5.','When the Deacons have entirely unclothed him, the Priests bring the holy oil of the anointing. Then he begins the anointing, through the threefold seal ing, and for the rest assigns the man to the Priests, for the anointing of his whole body, while himself on the Ecclesiastical Hierarchy .','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_SACRAMILLUMINATION_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_SACRAMENT_ILLUMINATION','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 2','Concerning things done in Illumination. WE have, then, reverently affirmed that this is the purpose of our Hierarchy, viz., our assimilation and union with God, as far as attainable. And, as the Divine Oracles teach, we shall attain this only by the love and the religious performance of the most worshipful Commandments.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_SACRAMMYRON_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_SACRAMENT_MYRON','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 4','Concerning sacerdotal Consecrations. SECTION I. SUCH, then, is the most Divine perfecting work of the Muron. But it may be opportune, after these Divine ministrations, to set forth the sacerdotal Orders and elections themselves, and thsir powers, and operations, and consecrations, and the triad of the superior ranks under them ; in order that the arrangement of our Hierarchy may be demonstrated, as entirely rejecting and excluding the disordered, the unreg','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_SACRAMSYNAXIS_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_SACRAMENT_SYNAXIS','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 3','Concerning things accomplished in the Synaxis. COURAGE, then, since we have made mention of this (Eucharist) which we may not pass over to celebrate any other Hierarchical function in pre ference to it. For according to our illustrious fc eiridxiiritcrts. u iiri''yvuva.i voepws.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_DIO_THEOSIS_DIONYS','ENT_DIO_THEOSIS','SRC_PSEUDO_DIONYSIUS_ECCLESIASTICAL_HIERARCHY','Pseudo-Dionysius, The Ecclesiastical Hierarchy','Hierarchy 1.3','Again, by the Deification from Itself, by the Divine likeness of many who become gods, ac cording to their several capacity, there seems, and is said to be, a distinction and multiplication of the One God, but He is none the less the Supreme God, and super-God, superessentially One God, - undivided in things divided, unified in Himself, both unmingled and unmultiplied in the many.','John Parker',1897,'https://archive.org/details/theworksofdionys00dionuoft',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1)
